  "construction": {
    "basis": "reconstruction",
    "fidelity": "not-applicable",
    "note": "The finished design was read from Brian Wichmann’s P70 vector drawing. The corners were snapped to exact values with the small star’s point radius as the unit. The drawing gives no steps. We devised the construction, sharing the unit-star and compass-transfer opening with the Meknes petal rosettes. The crossings R, V, W, X and Y1 to Y4 set the inner stars and outer pieces.",
    "changes": "The compass steps, their order and the named points are ours. OA is the small star’s point radius; the cell half-side is four radii plus three square diagonals. The finished tile edges follow the plain drawing. The palette is illustrative; no photograph was checked.",
    "reviewed": "2026-10-26"
  },
  "credits": [
    {
      "source": "Tiling Search, data21/P70: Bou Inania Madrasah, Meknes",
      "creator": "Brian Wichmann",
      "kind": "drawing",
      "url": "https://tilingsearch.mit.edu/HTML/data21/P70.html",
      "note": "Read from his finished drawing, not construction instructions. His references are David Wade, Pattern in Islamic Art (Studio Vista, 1976), page 70, and Wade photograph MOR 0909 of the Bou Inania madrasa, Meknes."
